There was the story just before the release of the Jensen, that the
engineers had to "detune" the machine, as it was too fast for the
(then) export controls.  The original machine had a 303.00 MHz
oscillator in it, for a CPU frequency of 151.5.  They had to cut
it back to 300.00 MHz (150.0 at the CPU) to meet export restrictions.

So, if you want 1% more, the system supposedly was qualified at that
speed.  Big deal...  :^(

You might be able to tweak a little more out of it than that as long
as you carefully control the environment (don't let the system get
anyplace close to it's max operating temperature.)  But the amount
you'll gain will probably be 5% or less.

More memory is the best bet.

Besides that, use it as a trade in on newer technology.  I've a 166
Mustang that runs circles around the 150 -- much more than just the
10% difference in CPU speed would indicate to the casual observer.

FWIW,
Aaron

