Good suggestions, Kevin. Let's see if key DEC people will respond. The 

ideal SMP tower config for Q1 96 would be quite like what you stated, 

except that the 21164A CPU could be pushed up to 533 MHz in volumes by 

that time - hope the new 0.35um CMOS runs fast. The 4 MB cache per CPU 

should be 133 MHz burst SRAMs, and 256-bit memory bus with 50 ns 66 MHz 

BEDO DRAM should give you 2 GB/s peak throughput - excellent for four 

21164A-533 or 21264 processors even without crossbar switching. Also, 

change FW SCSI for 40 MB/s Ultra Wide SCSI-3 or 200 MB/s FibreChannel. As 

the latter supports both SCSI-3 and ATM protocol, you can use it for 

ultrafast system interconnect without need for separate ATM. Finally, 

taking all this into account, I think realistic price for the config 

would probably be $49,900 - still pretty good for a 4 GFLOPS (peak) 

deskside machine the size of Gateway P5-120...



