I have a question about the Fortran 90 merge statement.

Consider the following Fortran 90 program:

      program merge_test
      integer,parameter:: n=100
      real,dimension(-n:n):: x,y
      integer:: i
      real:: s
      do i=-n,n
         x(i) = real(i)
      enddo
      y = merge(1.0/x,0.0,x.ne.0.0)
      s = sum(y)
      write(*,*) 'sum = ',s
      end

It works fine on an RS/6000 and a CM5, but on a Dec Alpha, I get

	forrtl: error (73): floating divide by zero

at merge statement.

Does the standard specify how the merge is implemented?  Is it legal to 
evaluate the true and false statements _before_  checking the conditional as 
the alpha compiler seems to be doing, or is the alpha compiler generating
incorrect code?

--

-Rodney James (rodney@oce.orst.edu)




