summary: DECstation 5000 locks up - DECNET suspected as cause
organization: Logica UK Ltd
keywords: DECNET lockup 5000 panic
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Has anyone ever come across a problem like the following, found the cause, or 
a solution?

When running DECNET 5.6.b on a DECstation 5000 running Ultrix 4.3
(ok so its out of date...bear with me)
configured on a WAN, it locks up after varying amounts of time, anything from 
1.5 hours upwards. 

Having removed all our bespoke software off the machine, and leaving it 
running, it still locks up - it just takes longer. Hence the assumption that 
there is a problem either with our DECNET configuration or with DECNET itself.

Before the crash (which may cause the machine to reboot, or just lock up) the 
machine reports (via 'vmstat' - 'b','avm' and 'fre' columns) that there is a 
sudden surge in locked processes; the cpu idle time converges to 100% and the 
virtual memory decreases rapidly. 
A 'cpu panic, locks held by cpu0 - print locks held by non active proccesses' 
is reported.

Anyway, would be grateful to hear from anyone who has experienced anything 
similar to this before. Oh - please, don't say 'why don't you just upgrade to 
the latest software....' - simple reason not to - its called 'money' ;-)

