On this system my .profile is a copy of a standard Athena profile.  It
calls several centralized Athena scripts which will call ~/.profile.mine
if I have one.  My .profile is not my own; some (but not all) of the
functionality of .profile has been moved to .profile.mine.  Similarly
my $ENV is not my own - I need to use .environment.  There are also
problems that I always have with csh scripts - they try to execute
my .environment which is a ksh file, not a csh file, because both
my .env (ksh) and .cshrc (csh) include it.

