RZ29 4 gig drives require a BA350 cabinet fan upgrade.  I had heard of
people only putting 4 gig drives in every other slot because of heat.
You can look at your drive's spec for typical power consumption which
is presented in watts.  There is a way to convert to BTU, but that probably
isn't useful.  I believe an RZ74 5.25" full height draws about 35 watts.
So 3 RZ74's would produce about as much heat as a 100 watt light bulb.
 
Most 3.5" SCSI disk drives seem to be in the 10 to 14 watt range.  So if
your 4 gig 3.5" drives spec out at 20 to 28 watts, then maybe your vendor
isn't pulling your leg.
 
Good Luck,  Doug



