In article <3q2ik3$kkd@jac.zko.dec.com>,
Stephen Hoffman <hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com> wrote:
>
>  LA75 reset sequence -- I don't have an LA50 manual handy -- is <ESC>c

<ESC>c is a general reset everything to saved settings, re-initialise 
hardware etc for nearly all DEC terminals & printers.  It's fundamentally
a hardware reset.

Often while it does this the device isn't listening to the serial port
and it will lose data.

Generally, using <ESC>c without taking into account that it's basically 
like turning the thing off & on is a Bad Idea.  There's usually a soft
reset instruction that will restore the device to a sane state without
being quite so brutal.  Otherwise, it's best to just send the sequences
that to set the device up the way you expect it.

Unfortunately, I can't find my Terminals & Printers handbook (the fount 
of all knowledge on this subject) right now so I can't say what it is.  
<sigh>

