I thought I knew about almost all the tuning & measurement tools on
the alpha, but I recently learned about two more that are documented
and easy to use.

uprofile and kprofile use the hardware performance counters to profile
user programs and the kernel. You can collect any of the following
counters.

If you're just trying to figure out why a program is slow, these tools
can help.



  Counter0Stats	  Counter1Stats
  _____________________________
  0disabled	  1disabled
  issues	  dcache
  pipedry	  icache
  loads		  dualissues
  pipefrozen	  mispredicts
  branches	  floatops
  cycles	  intops
  PALcycles	  stores
  nonissues	  novictims
  victims




