1.) How many VUPs is it in the single cpu (6200) configuration ? 

Each processor is 2.5 VUPS

2.) How difficult (or easy) is it to take a pair of 6220's and turn them
    into a single 6240 with four processors ? Is this supported ? Do you
    just remove the 2 cpu's from the one machine and insert them into the
    other ?

Yes, but VMS will require more license units.  You can't just load
both VMS base licenses into LMF.

3.) Is there a way to get it to go on single phase power ? The power
    supplies require the primary DC link (bus) to be about 300V. Does it
    matter how you get the 300V ? Can you modify the input rectifier to 
    give about 311VDC , from a 220V input , and run the power supplies
    off it? 

?

4.) Using a DWBUA ( BI to Unibus Adapter) is it possible to boot the machine
    off the Unibus? Is this supported ?

The Unibus was not supported as a boot device.  The console code is broken
and there were bugs in VMB.  When I was at Raytheon we modified the console
on our Mil-spec version and got DEC to fix VMB.  I don't know if the
VMB fixes ever got rolled into the released version of VMS.  You can boot
off a CIBCA, CIXCD, KDB50, KFMSA, or KZMSA if you have the latest and
greatest firmware.

5.) Whats the going price for a 6200 ?

Not much.  Any of the later VAXstations or MicroVaxes are a much better 
deal price, power, and maintanance wise.

Dave



