I did read the DSSI and alpha discussion with great interest we did use 6000 and 4000 vax systems using DSSI as main cluster and disk bus for many years with little to no problems. We use did shadow all the disk's and had no problems. We use FDDI as our backbone for lat decnet ... communication no problem. Now we use AXP 7000 systems with KFMSB's for cluster and disk communication ( we have lots of rf73 and rf74 disk's) now i see that we have crashes sometimes strange problemswith the DSSI buses DSSI disk's are served through the pedriver (FDDI or ethernet) instead of the DSSI so eg a systems looses "quorum disk watcher state's". Now is the time to investigate new disk platforms's we did look at the new HS rangedisk controllers and the new FSV disk controller. 
 First we wanted to buy the hsd30's but when we did read the story's about the KFMSB and our experience with it i don't think this is the platform to choose for. We hope to interface on the FDDI bus instead. 

