Some random answers:

  Digital UNIX and OpenVMS Alpha both contain built in support
  for the LK450 and LK411 keyboards.  No special software is needed.
  LK411 rev B or later keyboards need V6.1-1HW or later, or need
  a MUP to workaround a firmware change (also available on the net
  at http://www.service.digital.com/alpha/server/

  The LK411 and LK450 do not support a bell command, a VMS patch will
  be available shortly through the standard channels to ring the
  system bell.  This will be included in V6.2.

  The LK250 isn't supported on OpenVMS, and I suspect Digital Unix
  as well.  Use a LK411/450 instead.

  There is very little that will satisfy everyone regarding the
  placement of the ESC key.  I could make a lot of comments about
  it, but it would just start a holy war.

  As to NT or Warp (does anyone actually use OS2? ;-) I'm not sure
  what drivers are available.  I believe that there should be a NT
  driver for the LK450, not sure about the LK411.

