  The intent was to allow 1024x768 multisync SVGA monitors to work.
  I used a VS4000/60 this way for a while.  So have at it, that's
  what it's there for.

>Also, the machine is mouse-less.  Is the VSXXX-GA device a "standard"
>3-button mouse, or another DEC not-quite-standard one ?
>

  The mouse uses a DEC specified packet protocol and device ID
  response.  So, yes it's a DEC not-quite-standard mouse.  You can't
  plug anything else (except a tablet) into the connector.  In
  fact, the micro-DIN connector that is used is fairly uncommon,
  and the keying will prevent other mice (like a PC mouse) from
  being plugged in... which could be fatal to the mouse if not the
  system fuses.

