In article <801090368snz@acmenet.demon.co.uk>, 
john derbyshire <john@acmenet.demon.co.uk> writes:
>Can sonmebofy tell me what 'WCS does not match PCS' mean when booting
>a VAX11/780-5

I hope you didn't actually pay anything for this - the power bill alone
would make me shy away.

The 78x series (your 780-5 is a 780 that was field-upgraded to a 785 -
the different designation was necessary due to US FCC emissions rules)
has microcode in two places.  One is a set of PROMs - this is the PCS
(Program Control Store?) - the other is Writeable Control Store (WCS) that
is loaded from floppy.  Some microcode revisions required updating the
PCS.  My guess is that the console floppy you have is a version that is
incompatible with the PCS.  I don't know what you'd be able to do about
this.

How much is a 1.5 VUPS room heater worth to you, anyway?

