    [regarding memory SIMMs on AlphaStation systems ...]

> ... at least four installed to give you 128-bits
> of addressibility to processor's chipset.  

    Slight Correction ...

    The AlphaStation 250 has the 128-bit memory path, which requires SIMMS
    to be installed in sets of four.  The AlphaStation 200 and 400
    platforms use pairs of SIMMs for a 64-bit memory path.

    At the risk of boring you who have been paying attention, I have to
    reiterate that standard SIMMs that meet spec work fine -- but our
    Qualification Engineering group has found many memory parts that are
    out of spec.  Caveat emptor.

