I have a faculty member who is trying to get bootstrapped up to teach
COBOL in the fall on our 3000/600s machine currently running 2.0b. In
doing some experimenting, everytime he tries to access ISAM, he gets
a "not installed" error. EVERY Cobol compiler I've ever used included ISAM -
is this really an extra cost option on DEC Cobol? Or did we just goof the
install?

==forwarded message ==========
   COBOL programs to access files with indexed organization fail with
a "severe" error.  The text is "indexed file IO used, but ISAM is not 
installed.  

   In /usr/lib/cmplrs/cobol/relnotes there is a message to see the "Read 
Before Installing or Using DEC COBOL letter for specific information 
about required third-party software.  In another place (can't recall) I 
found a reference to the "Informix C-ISAM Library".

   I also found a file named libisam_stub.a in 
/usr/lib/cmplrs/cobol/cobolrtl.  

