        Perhaps  if  you  read  earlier  posts  in  this  thread, you'll
    understand  that people are asking for a _dedicated_ escape key.   I
    use VMS so I don't have their particular problem :-), but the key on
    my LK401-AA has a key cap marked so: +-----+
                                         |  ~  |
                                         |(ESC)|
                                         |  `  |
                                         +-----+
    While that key _may_ be  set  to  send  character  27, the user then
    needs  to  move the tilde and grave-accent elsewhere.   That  "else-
    where" winds up being on a key marked: +---+
                                           | > |
                                           | < |
                                           +---+
    And I seem to recall  mention  of some other difficulties...Dan?  In
    any  case,  no matter how misguided they may be :-), its seems  many
    users want an LK401-style keyboard with an _additional_,  dedicated,
    marked that way, escape key.  While I wouldn't use it, the fact that
    so  many  users want it (basically all unix users) and the fact that
    you can get such a layout in 3rd-party keyboards/terminals, seems to
    me sufficient reason to offer such a layout.

        VMS users don't need such a  thing,  but it doesn't get in their
    way  (my  3rd-party terminal at home is like that), so why not  give
    your customers what they want?  :-)

        -Ken
