>a multiheaded display when using two or three of the 
>*same* adapter in the slots.
>
>Is there any chance the X Server can support two different
>adapters?
>
>Today I replaced the HX with the TX adapter, and it works
>with the same X Server (Xdec). Should I try to install both
>adapters at the same time?
>
>Any ideas?

  You should be able to mix HX, CX and TX heads without any problem.

  HOWEVER the PXG won't coexist nicely with a second head.  It is
  due to some (ahem) bad programming practices from the MIPS days
  that assumed that nobody would ever have a dual-head system with
  a PXG as one of the heads.  I *have* made the PXG work with
  non-PXG additional heads, but it's thumbtacks and white glue.
  In addition, there were problems with 3D extensions when mixing
  2D and 3D heads... but these have been fixed in the newer 3D
  adapter code.


