If they are running the FlexLM license management package (which is
getting pretty common these days) the host id is simply the physical
address of your network interconnect card.  You can find out what that
is by looking at your /var/adm/messages file (at the end) and look for
the string where the ethernet (or FDDI) device driver gets loaded.
The default physical address will be a string of 8 bytes, in hex.
For DEC controllers it starts out 08-00-2b.

