Jerry Lugert (jerry@bennyhana) wrote:

: I picked up a multiflow trace at an auction last week. It's a 64bit, .5GB RAM,
: 5GB drive 89 vintage bsd 4.3 machine. Besides this I know nothing about it.
: Is there anyone out there who knows what this thing is?

Yes, I've got one in my basement with a bad power supply. Mine is a 7/200,
the bottom of the line, for $200,000 university price.  Yours apparently
has two "processors", so it is really a 512-bit very-long-instruction-word
computer.  Mine has only one proc, so is a 128-bit vliw machine.  Yours
executes 4 integer and 2 FP operations every cycle, which is at 33 MHz.
The big problem is the machine is wired for 3 phase, although there is
nothing in the machine that actually uses 3 phase power.  Also, the power
supplies are WAY overrated!  It will be necessary to rewire the big
black module in the bottom, which contains power distribution and the
"environment processor", which is the console computer and monitors
cooling and power.  It should be fairly easy to make the system run from
220 V single phase power, but it throws off a lot of heat!  Several
KW, at least.  I do have a set of Multiflow OS manuals, plus some
manuals on the VME I/O cards.  Multiflow wouldn't give us any info on
their hardware at all.  then they went bankrupt.  I'm sure I could swap
out the VME supply, but I'm not sure it is worth the time.  Let me know
what's going on with your machine.

				Jon




