Some weeks ago I wrote:

] After upgrading two 5900/240 (KN03 CPU: 40 MHz R3000) with DEFZA FDDI 
] interfaces in a standalone ring configuration (DECconcentrator 500) to
] 5900/260 (KN05 CPU: 60 MHz R4400) we have performance problems
] on the FDDI ring due to interface input errors:
] With high workload on the ring (either NFS or TCP) between the two
] machines there are intermittent interface input errors on the fza0
] interface (DEFZA), especially on the destination interface (which
] has the higher input data rate).
] These input errors disturb network performance such that it is roughly half
] of the maximum possible performance extrapoltated from short
] undisrupted tests:
] around 2 MB/sec for TCP instead of the extrapolated 5 MB/sec.
] 
] When there were the slower KN03 CPUs in the systems we did not
] see these input errors. I even swapped back these KN03
] CPUs after discovering the problem with the KN05 CPUs and made
] havy tests: not even one intput error and smooth transfers!
] 
] So it looks like there is a timing problem in the fza driver in
] Ultrix/RISC 4.4.
] 
] Is this problem known ? Are there any patches for Ultrix/RISC 4.4 ?
] How do we get these patches (we are in Germany/Europe).

Later on I added (after being asked about firmware revisions):

] I forgot to mention: the DEFZA boards give the following output
] when asked about firmware:
] diamant> netstat -s -I fza0
] [...]
] fza0 FDDI characteristics 
] 
] Link Address:                      08-00-2B-35-C5-74
] Firmware Revision:                 1.2 
] ROM Revision:                      1.1 
] SMT Version ID:                    1   
] [...]

] I found no mention of newer firmware in the relaese notes I have.


