: Is there anyone out there who knows what this thing is?

Yes.  The multiflow was the first commericial realization of the Very Long
Instruction Word architecture.  A Trace 14 would have been the midrange
machine.  The compiler which makes the thing work fast was derived at
Yale (Bulldog compiler).

Anyhow, Multiflow has been out of business for five years or so.  Bell
Atlantic was trying to sell these things at 10 cents on the dollar (buy
one get nine free) a few years back.  If it runs, it's a neat machine,
but don't try to get support for it.

Almost bought one at Rutgers.

-Ron




