  Actually, I was at a meeting with Wes Melling (the VMS Business Segment
  VP) were he was convinced to re-evaluate the Basic question. The 
  problem, as I understand it, is that there are only small (if any) 
  differences between the Visual C/C++ and Digital's C/C++ dialects. This 
  allows the NT sources to be easily re-compiled under VMS. Then, given a 
  library of NT-API calls, one can create a NT equivalent VMS image.

  However, the differences between Visual Basic and DEC's Basic are rather
  extensive (as Jeff pointed out to me). Assuming someone, be it Digital or
  some savy ISV, comes up with a new  Digital Basic that's compatible with 
  the Visual Basic dialect - this problem would be resolved.

