injury. I suspect that a machine used for industrial control could cause 
both of those.
But, I make sure all my home machines are kept in as near original 
condition as possible. This does not mean I refuse to put in any 'modern' 
spares - if a chip fails it gets replaced, and I don't care about the 
date code. It does mean that the machine has to work at least as well as 
it did when it left the factory. Any faults, no matter how minor, get 
corrected.


