I'll have to agree with that. I've not found a single 'professional' 
repairman who can do a proper repair. I don't mean that he replaces 
unnecessary parts (i.e. he swaps boards rather than components), but that 
after a repair, I often have to spend a few hours correcting things 
before the machine runs properly again.

As a hobbyist, I know my machines internally. I know what all the chips 
