On 10 May 1995, Holger Burde wrote:

> Hi,
> 
> We use SUNs PCNFS to integrate PC's into TCP/IP based LANs. With some new 
> MicroSoft Products, we got Problems storing/retrieving files from the 
> networkdrive.
> 
> Since we sell a kind of Databaseapplication and most other applications
> need file/recordlocking, we use the lockmanager (NFS on Unix Server) and
> mount Directorys _allways_ with the /MS Option. Soo it's of _no_ use for us 
> if it works with /NS. 
> 
> Q: - Why do we get this errors and only with newer MS-Produkts using OLE2
>      Docs ?
>    - Is there any solution to this nasty problem ? 
>    - Someone told us about OL2.0 making locking request with 4GB
>      offsets (NFS is 32 Bit, so files are only 2GB). Do we have to
>      get a storage.dll version 2.01 which uses 2GB offsets to help 
>      clients like mac (2GB filesize) or NFS (all OLE2 IO is done 
>      via this dll) ?
>      (the 4GB request is done for some 'technical' reasons ...)
>    - the server is an AXP (with OSF/1 3.0). Is this probably a problem
>      with the DEC implementation of NFS ? (dec sucks ?) 
>    - is someone doing 'MS Officeworks' in such an environment
>      without Problems ? 
> 
> PS   A test with Word 2.0b gives no error ! 
> 
> thanx in advance
> 
> hb
> 
> #######################################################################
> dipl. inform. h.b.
> j03k@zfn.uni-bremen.de
> voice: 049-0421-444 285
> ####################################################################### 

	 According to a few people on the net and some companies that build
NFS products, this is an identified bug in the MS OLE package.  It is not
a result of you NFS server (we serve from a Solaris-based Sparcstation
with similar problems).  It seems to appear in both the Mac and PC OLE
implementations.  I have not heard of any word from Microsoft on when or
if they intend to fix the problem.  For all we know, they could be using
this problem to push Windows NT, which I have heard, is not subject to the
error. 

	However, some of the Mac and PC NFS vendors have been providing client
workarounds.  We were able to get an upgrade for NFS/Share for our Mac,
and it has been happily reading and writing Word and Excel files to an NFS
volume for over a month now with no problems so far (this was impossible
before the upgrade). 
 
	Although, in this case, the error was the result of an application
and not the NFS client, I would not suggest using PCNFS.  It is reportedly
very buggy and support from SunSoft can be frustrating.  Instead, we use
Beame and Whitsides BWNFS and have had very few problems with it.  Almost
every problem we have had with it has been a result of a server bug
(Solaris has plenty), an appication/environment bug (incorrect Windows
configurations or this MS-OLE bug), or simply "pilot-error" (ie something
I set up wrong despite there being very clear instructions in the manual
and/or on-line).  Also, unlike SunSoft, B&W's product line is made up of
very few network products of which their support staff seem to be very
knowledgeable. 

