In article <shepherd.95May12134353@pathfinder>, shepherd@suite.com writes:
:Anyone know where I can get some information on building vmsinstal kits.
Documentation or a live expert would be ideal. I've attempted to clone
from other kits but am getting an error message on installation of my
kit that is not particularly helpful.

   There is a Developer's Guide to VMSINSTAL manual available from Digital,
   and a copy of this manual is on the Consolidated On-line Documentation
   CD-ROM.  (This manual is part of the optional documentation, and can be
   ordered as part of an optional documentation set, or seperately under
   part AA-PWBXA-TE.)

   Also available are the POLYCENTER Software Installation Developer's and
   User's Guides -- PCSI is part of OpenVMS starting in V6.1.

   If you decide to use VMSINSTAL, I would *strongly* recommend seperating
   the software "installation" from the software "site-specific tailoring"
   tasks, as this will make a future migrating to PCSI *much* easier.  In
   effect, I would avoid doing any sort of site-specific configuration as
   part of the installation, rather, I would relegate all of this work (if
   and when this is necessary) to a fac$CONFIG procedure.

   PCSI manuals are also available.

