:so how I go about trading in this *&^%$ PC keyboard?

  The AlphaStations can be ordered with one of the Digital-traditional
  LK-series keyboard (the LK411-xx; I'm told folks have used the older
  LK450-xx with some success, too), and, of course, with one of the 101
  or 102 key PC keyboards (PCXAL-xx).

  The keyboard plug on the AlphaStations is the 6 pin mini-DIN that
  is used on PCs, and is (obviously) not compatible with the RJ-series
  connectors used on the LK201 and LK401 keyboards.

  One can order these keyboards from the folks at 1-800-DIGITAL, or from
  your local Digital office or Digital distributor.

