Subject: DISPLAY on Alpha/OSF
Date: 1995/05/09
Message-ID: <3oof1s$bn7@newshost.lanl.gov>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 102296410
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: Los Alamos National Laboratory
x-url: news:comp.sys.dec
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 1.1S (X11; I; IRIX 5.3 IP22)

Is there a way to automatically set the DISPLAY variable when logging
into a remote Alpha running OSF? I log into an Alpha frequently from
a variety of other machines (SGI's) and want to avoid manually
setting the display to the machine I am logging in from. Any help would
be appreciated.

On SGI's, the following code in your .login works:


  if ($?DISPLAY == 0) then
      if ($?REMOTEHOST) then
          setenv DISPLAY ${REMOTEHOST}:0
      else
          setenv DISPLAY :0
      endif
  endif


But it does not work on the Alpha (because $REMOTEHOST is not set).




