:Firstly, please excuse my ignorance of all matters VAX/DEC.

  I'll assume you mean OpenVMS, as various VAX systems can run OpenVMS
  and (in various cases) ULTRIX, as well as a few other operating systems.
  I'll further assume that you have OpenVMS systems on both ends of the
  IP connection.

:I have two sites connected by IP, both have clients but only one site has
:some servers that need to be accessed via DECnet.  I really need to access
:these servers from the other site and guess this can be done via some
:form of
:tunneling.  I know there is a product called TCPware but this would need
:to be installed on 'servers' at each end and I don't have this situation.
:What I'm really looking for is either a small black-box or some software
:to run under U*ix.  For our very limited traffic, the cheaper the
:better.

  There's no need to "tunnel" -- DECnet runs quite nicely over an IP
  transport -- DECnet OSI V6.0 and later support this capability.  You
  will, of course, need a DECnet OSI node on each end of the IP network
  connection, and these nodes will have to be running one of the various
  IP packages available for OpenVMS.

  Digital, TWG, TGV, and various other organizations market IP packages.

