We got three AlphaStation 250-4/266 boxes in today & they're up in
running. My comments follow:

They're fast. I'm using a 400-4/233 for my desktop and these were
noticable faster. Too bad my students will be using them and not me.

I don't know about other 200-series boxes, but the power and reset
switch are right up front, just waiting to be accidently poked. I view
this as a design flaw myself. I like the corresponding power/reset on
HP machines - power signals a shutdown of the system.

The "key lock" on the back of the system was jammed on all three of
the systems. It took a lot work to get the key in there (like, pushing
*really hard*). We're not taking the keys out of the locks, because we
don't know if we'll be able to open them again. This was surprising.




