        The FAQ deals with MAIL  forwarding,  as  does the internal HELP
    within  VMS MAIL (did you try that?).  However, since Internet-style
    domain addresses are not native to VMS MAIL, you'll  need  to  check
    your system to see what "prefix" to use in the following.  Typically
    it will be SMTP%, IN% or MX%, but others are possible.  Now, without
    going  into  the  reasons for needing _three_ _sets_ of double-quote
    marks, do the following (substituting your  userid and DEC UNIX host
    name, I've used the address in your sig for the example):

        $ mail
        MAIL> set forward SMTP%"""mike@snowhite.eeap.cwru.edu"""
        MAIL> exit
        $

