newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec

   Since the last December when I installed mbone staffs (AF, sd, vat, 
nv, wb...) in our DEC 3000-600 running OSF/1 V2.0B, I experienced  
frequent system "panic" on our OSF/1.

   "trap: invalid memory read access from kernel mode"

  I called the local DEC service and they brought back and analyzed 
the  crash dump files for 4 crashes.    ** After 4 months **  they 
(DEC) concluded that:

> This look like a bbadriver problem.  Here's the stack trace from
> the crash-data file:
>    :
> DMA buffers allocated using kalloc was not always returning 
> contiguous memory.  IOCTRL ASIC DMA buffers must be contiguous.
> Solution was to allocate 1 page buffers at a time instead of 
> all at once.
> -------------------------------------------------------------------
> Fixed in pre. BL12.  This crash was running T3.0-2 (BL11).

   Local DEC service told us that this bug of bbadriver (sound driver) 
has been fixed in OSF V3.0 and they recommended to upgrade OS from OSF 
V2.0B to OSF V3.0 or latter.

   In the beginning of the last April, we have upgraded the operating 
system of our AXP to OSF/1 V3.0B  (Rev. 358.78) according to the 
suggestions of DEC.

   However, we still  experienced the "panic" after this version up.  
Here I show some records in /usr/var/adm/crash/crash-data.*

(1)CASE 1  (in OSF/1 V3.0B  Rev. 358.78)

     trap: invalid memory read access from kernel mode
     
   0 boot(0x0, 0x4, 0xff000a0a30336532, 0x0, 0x0) ["../../../../src
     /kernel/arch/alpha/machdep.c":1499, 0xfffffc00004460e8]
   1 panic(s = 0xfffffc00005339e0 = "kernel memory fault") ["../../..
     /../src/kernel/bsd/subr_prf.c":668, 0xfffffc00004092a4]
   2 trap() ["../../../../src/kernel/arch/alpha/trap.c":1262, 
     0xfffffc0000453a30]
   3 _XentMM(0x4, 0xfffffc000031aa84, 0xfffffc0000569c50, 0xffffffff
     8cc4f000, 0xffffffff8cb35f02) ["../../../../src/kernel/arch/alpha/
     locore.s":1256, 0xfffffc00004432f4]
   4 freeb(mp = 0xffffffff8cb1e600) ["../../../../src/kernel/streams/
      str_memory.c":561, 0xfffffc000031aa80]
   5 bba_Voice_Write(0xffffffff8cb1e6e8, 0xffffffff8cb35f02, 0xffffffff8
     cb1e688,0xffffffff8ccde540, 0xfffffc0100000040) ["../../../../src/
     kernel/io/dec/tc/amd79c30.c":2754, 0xfffffc00004c159c]
   6 bba_txintr(0xffffffff8ccde500, 0xfffffc00004bb2a4, 0xffffffff
     90c0314b, 0xa,0xfffffc00004c231c) ["../../../../src/kernel/io/dec
     /tc/amd79c30.c":2785, 0xfffffc00004c16b4]
   7 bbaintr(0x0, 0xd, 0xfffffc000059d7e4, 0xb25c22f976a96, 0xfffffc00
     004639f4)["../../../../src/kernel/io/dec/tc/amd79c30.c":3171, 
     0xfffffc00004c2574]
         :

(2)CASE 2  (in OSF/1 V3.0B  Rev. 358.78)

     panic (cpu 0); freeing free mblk

   0 boot(0x0, 0x4, 0xfffffc00004c8ac4, 0x5d9622fa97b4f, 0xfffffc000020
     9ec0)  ["../../../../src/kernel/arch/alpha/machdep.c":1499, 
     0xfffffc00004460e8]
   1 panic(s = 0xfffffc0000515c70 = "freeing free mblk") ["../../../..
     /src/kernel/bsd/subr_prf.c":668, 0xfffffc00004092a4]
   2 freeb(mp = 0xffffffff8cc5f600) ["../../../../src/kernel/streams/
     str_memory.c":562, 0xfffffc000031aa9c]
   3 bba_Voice_Write(0xffffffff8cbd0ae8, 0xffffffff8cb36f02, 0xffffffff
     8cbd0a88,0xffffffff8cb82f40, 0xfffffc0100000040) ["../../../../src/
     kernel/io/dec/tc/amd79c30.c":2754, 0xfffffc00004c159c]
   4 bba_txintr(0xffffffff8cb82f00, 0xfffffc00004bb2a4, 0xffffffff
     90c03421, 0xa,0xfffffc00004c231c) ["../../../../src/kernel/io/dec/
     tc/amd79c30.c":2785, 0xfffffc00004c16b4]
   5 bbaintr(0x0, 0xd, 0xfffffc000059d7e4, 0x5d9622fa97b4f, 0xfffffc0
     0004639f4)["../../../../src/kernel/io/dec/tc/amd79c30.c":3171, 
     0xfffffc00004c2574]
         :

   It seems that these problems are cased by bba_Voice_Write calling in
both cases and due to a bug of bbadriver in OSF V3.0B.  I have already 
sent the complete dump files in /usr/var/adm/crash to DEC service in 
Japan in the last month.  But still no answer.

   Does anyone know the patch for this bug ?  Is there any suggestions ?
Thanks for the information.

