In article <1995May5.074130.32@thehulk>, munroe@dmc.com writes:
:I'm trying to get a KFQSA to work with an old microvax II in a
:world box I use for testing hardware.  I can't get the uvax to
:boot with the new board in it.
:
:I bought the board used and I haven't been able to find any
:information about configuring the board anywhere.  As near as I
:can see, there is only one set of 4 slider switchs available for
:configuration.  Has anybody out there been successful in putting
:this board into:

  You will need the manual for the KFQSA device, as the KFQSA CSR and
  interrupt vector need to be set to reflect the current Q-bus system
  configuration and the number of DSSI devices present.  You may/wil
  need to change the CSR and interrupt vector(s) setting(s) on one or
  more other devices present in the Q-bus, as well -- this means you
  may need the manuals for one or more other devices, as well.

  The KFQSA installation and user guide: EK-KFQSA-IN

  There are two common mistakes made when dealing with the Q-bus.  The
  first is neglecting to consider *all* devices in the Q-bus, as a
  change to one Q-bus device can cause a cascading changes to the CSR
  and vector settings on other devices.  The second is the misconception
  that the interrupt vector setting displays produced by a SYSGEN SHOW
  command are the actual settings -- SYSGEN shows the desired/required
  settings, not the actual settings.  (One must pull the Q-bus boards
  out and decode the interrupt vector settings to know for sure...)

