Additional Information:


Major duties of the Computer Systems Manager include the following:

*  Maintain operating system and utility program software.
*  Manage vendor-supplied software licenses and support contracts.  Build 
   and maintain productive relationships with vendor partners.
*  Ensure the security of systems and the information residing on them, and
   manage plans for the recover and continued operation of such systems in
   the event of catastrophe.
*  Monitor system performance and capacity and provide recommendations for
   ongoing renewal and replacement of system resources.
*  Respond to system problems.  Provide minor or routine hardware
troubleshooting.
*  Work closely with the Networking group to provide network support on
   centralized systems.
