The DSP3160 guide I have has PRELIMINARY marked all over it,
and doesn't say anything about DSP3160A, but here is what it has
for termination (note:  the drawings are not very detailed):


	The DSP3160 is capable of supplying termination power
	to the SCSI bus through the TERMPWR signal on the bus.
	In addition, the drive can be configured to provide active
	termination to the SCSI bus.  The figure below shows the
	proper jumper arrangements for each terminator power
	configuration.

	Active termination should be enabled ONLY if the drive
	is at the end of the SCSI bus.

                                                    |
                                          +-----+ O |
                                          | o o |   |
                                          | o o |   |
                                          | o o |   |
                                          +-----+   |
                  -------------------------------------+
                  |      SCSI Connector                |
                  -------------------------------------+

               +-----+
               | === |	Drive provides power to SCSI TERMPWR.
               | o o |  Active termination disabled.
               | o o |
               +-----+

               +-----+
               | o o |  No drive power provided to SCSI TERMPWR.
               | o o |  Active termination is enabled.
               | === |
               +-----+

               +-----+
               | === |  Drive provides power to SCSI TERMPWR.
               | o o |  Active termination is enabled.
               | === |
               +-----+

               +-----+
               | o o |  No drive power provided to SCSI TERMPWR.
               | o o |  Active termination is disabled.
               | o o |
               +-----+

-- 

(Whatever you do, don't quote me on that.)
