Subject: Answer : Windows/NT with ATI Mach64 video controller ?
Date: 1995/05/03
Message-ID: <3MAY95.10191894@mve.neurophys.wisc.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 101996776
organization: Dept of Neurophysiology - UW Madison USA
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



     A couple of days ago I asked if it was possible to run Windows/NT
     on an Alphastation 4/100 configured for VMS with an ATI Mach64
     graphics controller. Thanks to Tom Hospod and Rich Dischler of
     DEC for providing a prompt answer, which is : 

       Yes, you can run Windows/NT, VMS and Digital-Unix all with
       the same ATI Mach64 video board. What you need are different
       software drivers, which are apparently available from DEC
       customer service centers. For example, the Win/NT driver is
       available as part # AK-QHC1A-CA. This driver will also be
       be included in future versions of the NT CD-rom at some later
       date. For Unix, the driver support is built into the OS kernel.

     I should add as an aside that if you plan to switch back and forth
     between VMS and Win/NT you would apparently need two separate system
     discs to boot from.

     Hope this is useful information for someone else.

     Ravi Kochhar
     University of Wisconsin - Madison
     kochhar@neurophys.wisc.edu
     5/3/95



