> 
> I am having difficulty loading an LPS32 from an HP-UX host.
...
>  - But the printer never responds.

Hello Jeff.
The LPS's rely on the SQE (heartbeat) signal being enabled on the ethernet
tranceiver for the booting via MOP to work. The first time it happened to
us, we where baffled. running VMS, and all. And all we did was shutting
it of momentarily for maintenance. All boot requests getting to the boot
server, server replying, but the LPS not listening.
Found out that sometime during the past halfyear they swapped netgear, and
then replacing the old tranceiver with a new one wich had SQE disabled.
They said that *** (Some big un*x vendor other than DEC) had recommended
them to disable SQE on all tranceivers to be on the safe side. Some advice!
MOP requires SQE, but DECNET and TCP don't. Funny, huh? :-)
Good luck!
/Johan Jansson
erajj@kiera.ericsson.se



