In article <1MAY95.15520011@mve.neurophys.wisc.edu>,
kochhar@mve.neurophys.wisc.edu (Ravi Kochhar) writes:
>
>  Hi,
>
>   We are planning to buy an Alphastation 4/100 (VMS version). It
>   comes with the ATI Mach 64 controller. It is implied that this
>   video controller is supported only under VMS, and for Windows/NT
>   DEC sell the same machine with a different controller (DE864 ??).
>
>   The question is, if we buy the VMS version with the ATI Mach64
>   controller now, will this prevent us from later installing
>   and running Windows/NT on this system ?
>

  The ATI Mach64 CX (2mb DRAM) is supported by OpenVMS Alpha, and
  Digital UNIX.  NT support is provided by the option vendor, and
  if you find the option on the Hardware Compatability List, then
  it's supported by NT.  My belief is that the card is on the HCL,
  but I'll confirm it later today.

  OpenVMS does not support the DEC864 (S3 Vision864 card) yet...
  look for it late summer to early fall.

  OpenVMS V6.2 will support both the ATI Mach64 CX and GX (VRAM)
  cards with 1-4mb of memory on them.  Digital will only sell the
  CX card, but users can purchase the other cards off-the-shelf.

