each of the licensing schemes have their good/bad points and they all
got stuff you need to type in (except when someone is nice enough to
send you the stuff already in the right file, ready to go). I've never liked
the the licensing schemes that tie the licenses to a particular machine (by 
some annoying unique identifier like the hardware ethernet address - 
real fun when your ethernet board goes south and the technician forgets
to swap address ROMs when he replaces the board) or by system ID. I've had
no end of hassle trying to convince companies that, no, I'm not trying to
steal your software by moving it to another machine - the machine it
was running on is gone - they always seem to end up wanting some
incredible amount of red-tape from upper management testifying to the fact
that we aren't stealing their stuff... yech...

