each raster line on a new line, using a normal text editor.  This
works better than you might think - you can get a reasonable idea
of what the character will look like on the terminal.  If you don't
have PL/I, you can always write a simple macro in C that will do
something very much like this, or failing that, a preprocessor that
will take a file with 0's and 1's (or * and - or whatever you like
for the foreground and background characters) and write out the
appropriate initializations in Fortran or whatever other language
you're using.  If you're interested in a C macro to do this, I can
probably dig one up that I wrote a while back.

There may well be more sophisticated tools.  But unless your needs
are fairly heavy-duty, this is likely to be all you'll need.

Bruce C. Wright



