C O M P U T E R   S Y S T E M S   M A N A G E R
Oberlin College

The Irvin E. Houck Computing Center at Oberlin College invites applications for
the position of Computer Systems Manager.  This is a full-time position
reporting 
to the Director of Administrative Computing Services.  The Computer Systems 
Manager also works closely with the members of the Client Services,
Operations, and Networking groups.

The Computer Systems Manager is responsible for technical administration and
support of centralized computer systems (both special-purpose servers and 
multi-user timesharing systems).  Major duties include system and utility
software 
maintenance, system security maintenance, system performance and capacity 
planning, troubleshooting, support of network software residing on these
systems,
and support of operations and networking staffs.

The candidates of most interest will display the following qualities:

*  A proven record of providing first-class user and technical support.
   Demonstrated ability to work well with a diverse client population and 
   to function as a member of a professional team.

*  Excellent writing and speaking skills.  Demonstrated ability to craft 
   technical reports and proposals.

*  A minimum of 2 to 4 years experience managing DEC VAX and Alpha computer 
   systems running VMS, OpenVMS, and OSF/1 operating systems.

*  Experience working with systems in ethernet and Internet network 
   environments and in providing support of network software such as mailers 
   and nameservers.

*  Well-developed programming skills, preferably in C.

*  Planning and organizational skills, including the ability to plan, manage,
   and execute complex technical projects.

Oberlin College is a highly selective liberal arts college of 2800 students 
located in the rural environment of northeastern Ohio, yet having convenient 
access to metropolitan Cleveland.  The college provides a competitive salary
commensurate with experience, plus attractive benefits which include a generous
pension program, medical and long-term disability insurance, one month annual
vacation, life insurance, and tuition support for children.

Screening of candidates will begin on May 17, 1995 and will continue until 
the position is filled. Applications, including a complete resume, 
3 professional references, and salary requirements should be directed to:
  Michael Dieckmann
      Irvin E. Houck Computing Center
      Oberlin College
      Oberlin, OH  44074
      internet:  bmike@ocvaxc.cc.oberlin.edu
      FAX:  216-775-8573

Oberlin College is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity employer.  Women 
and members of minority groups are particularly encouraged to apply.
=====================
Additional Information:


Major duties of the Computer Systems Manager include the following:

*  Maintain operating system and utility program software.
*  Manage vendor-supplied software licenses and support contracts.  Build 
   and maintain productive relationships with vendor partners.
*  Ensure the security of systems and the information residing on them, and
   manage plans for the recover and continued operation of such systems in
   the event of catastrophe.
*  Monitor system performance and capacity and provide recommendations for
   ongoing renewal and replacement of system resources.
*  Respond to system problems.  Provide minor or routine hardware
troubleshooting.
*  Work closely with the Networking group to provide network support on
   centralized systems.
*  Work closely with the Operations staff to provide operational support on
   centralized systems.
*  Provide technical support on systems and utility software to other groups
   of the Computing Center and to external clients.  Assist the Help Desk
   in resolving systems concerns.
*  Act as electronic mail postmaster on several systems.


Oberlin's central systems environment includes the following:

*  VAX 6000-620 system running VMS.
*  VAX 6000-420 system running OpenVMS.
*  VAXStation 4000-90 development system running VMS.
*  VAXstation 3100-76 console system.
*  DECstation 2100 usenet news server running Ultrix.
*  Alpha 3000-300 world-wide web server running OSF/1.

Oberlin is a computing-intensive highly-networked environment connected 
to the global Internet.  The campus-wide data network is based on an FDDI 
backbone with intra-building ethernet.  All central academic and 
administrative buildings are fully-networked, and this summer Oberlin will 
begin a 2-year project to network all student residence halls.  The desktop 
computing environment consists primarily of Apple Macintosh, multi-vendor 
DOS/Windows, and Unix workstation platforms.


Current system management projects include the following:

*  Installation of a new campus-wide electronic mail system.
*  Replacement/upgrade of the academic VAX system.
*  Replacement/upgrade of the usenet news server.
*  Establishment of a computer systems continuity plan for emergency
   operation of mission-critical systems.
*  Establishment of automated operations and management procedures for
   several tasks.
*  Planning for replacement of the administrative VAX system.
*  Training and professional development of computer operators.

