I am having difficulty loading an LPS32 from an HP-UX host.
The HP-UX is running DEC PrintServer Software for HP-UX Systems,
Version 4.2.
The HP 9000/700 is running 8.07.

The primary system image successfully downloads to the printer.
The printer then request secondary boot images and configuration
files via a BOOTP request. 
The HP-UX system responds with a BOOTP reply.
The printer then sends an ARP request for it's address.
The printer then sends an DECnet IV Ethernet Endnode Hello.
The printer then sends an ICMP Address Mask Request.
The printer then responds to the ARP request.
A system responds with the correct mask for the network.
The printer then sends a DEC MOP Remote Console packet.
The HP-UX system then attempts a connection on TCP port 170.
 - But the printer never responds.


We have followed the Troubleshooting Procedures in Section 8 of the
PrinteServer Management guide to no avail.
The only way that we can currently load the printer, is by enabling bridging
on the cisco routers between a VMS host and the printer and loading the
printer via DEC MOP from the VMS host.

Does anyone know what the content of the BOOTP reply should be; with emphasis
on the Vendor Specified Data?  Is this the proper sequence for secondary 
load?  

BTW: We have loaded this printer from this HP-UX system in the past. Things
that have changed since the last succesful load.
1. Zmail was loaded.
2. Changed the DECnet node number.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.





