sherouse@RadOnc.MUSC.EDU (George W. Sherouse, Ph.D.) writes:

>The situation:

> So now the Alpha mounts the user
>directories using NFS.  Since the change, anno goes into a suspended
>state every time it is invoked by mh-e or xmh.

>Smells to me like a problem with NFS mounts from SGI to DEC, perhaps
>related to file locking.  Unfortunately, this is exactly the kind of
>bug that neither SGI nor DEC is gonna help squash ("We don't support
>MH.").  Anybody got a clue?

Our problem report machine lost a disk, so I can't check today, but
I don't think we've seen a bug report.  We do fix mh problems.  Well,
some of them.

What version of NFS are you using?  If you have OSF/1 V3.0 or higher
and Irix 5.3 you're probably using NFS V3 (the mount command on OSF
will tell you).  If that's the case, try NFS V2 (mount with -o nfsv2).
SGI forgot to implement Network Lock Manager Protocol V4, which is
required for NFS V3.  (I.e. file locking doesn't work if SGI and
NFS V3 is involved.)
