In <KUGE.95May2125112@k1ss.strl.nhk.or.jp> kuge@strl.nhk.or.jp (Tetsuro KUGE) writes:

>Hi, speedsters (^^;),
>
>It is seemed the access to char *array on Alpha CPU
>is NOT so faster than the "slower" chips of Sparc etc.
>
>On the Alpha server 4/275 with OSF/1 V.3.0B,
>the cc opitons -O* does not improve the situation (:-<).
>
>Is it my misunderstanding ?

It's not your misunderstanding, it's the Alpha architecture not being
able to access bytes.  The only data sizes that can be directly accessed
by Alpha are 32 and 64 bit.  For characters and short int's there is a
certain overhead, as the accesses have to be implemented in software (with
more than one instruction :-)

Dan
