It may not be exactly of the vintage you want, but you'll find
some useful information at the anonymous ftp site

    sunsite.unc.edu

in the directory

    /pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/hardware

where I've been archiving data related to Q-bus and Unibus hardware.
Most of the stuff concerns PDP-11's, but of course there's a fair
amount of overlap with VAXen.  In particular, you'll find the file
"field-guide.txt" to be extremely useful in identifying all sorts of
Q-bus and Unibus hardware.  (The VCB02 and KA630 are mentioned there.)

At the same site, you'll also find some very useful information
culled from DECUServe conferences. In the directory

    /pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/decusdocs

you'll find several megabytes of helpful information, again dealing
mainly with older hardware (up to the late 80's, mostly, but
there's a little bit of newer stuff).

An excellent reference to DEC's RD series of drives can be found at
the anonymous ftp site

    ftp.spc.edu

where in the home directory (i.e. [ANONYMOUS] ) you'll find a file
named "THIRD-PARTY-DISKS.TXT".

