In article <1995Apr27.092724.8387@malad2.mala.bc.ca>, dunnett@mala.bc.ca (Malcolm Dunnett) writes:
>
>We are having a rather strange problem with a Datatrieve procedure.
>
>At the point where the procedure is attempting to do a "DEFINE FILE"
>to create a data file for a temporary domain we get the following error:
>
>%CDD-F-NOWRITE, no privilege to write SYS$SYSDEVICE:[CDDPLUS]
>Reinitializing CDD 
>
>This strikes me as particularly odd since the "DEFINE FILE" command only
>creates a data file, it doesn't make any changes to the CDD. ...

True.  Unfortunately, DTR was starting a read/write transaction to the
dictionary, not a read only transaction for the DEFINE FILE command.
I sent in an SPR, and consistent with the DTR group's commitment to 
a quality product, it was fixed in the next release, 7.0.  I wish 
all software were supported as well as DTR.

Upgrade DTR to V7.0, keep Rdb where it is, and all should be well.

