A friend of mine who services some PDP-11's for the area school systems came
to me with a box of TK50's that had been in a fire safe when the school
burned down.  The poor 11/73 was toasted so bad that the only thing left was
of the disk drove was the hub - the platters had melted.  The temperature in
the safe apparently had gone up to over 200 degrees F, and as a result the
TK50's seem to have lost the calibration marks somewhere in the middle of
the tape. I stuck the tapes (written in RSTS 9.5 backup) in my VAX TK drive,
and all the tapes report position lost error when we try to go restore the 
tape. (anal/err reports a data synchronization error - see below)

They had no off-site backups, so these tapes are it.

So, is there any hope of recovery of these tapes?  

Can anybody recommend any particular company from experience? (Ontrack, 
Advanced Data Recovery, etc.)






