  As I mentioned to you earlier (and is worth repeating for our at-home 
audience 8-), normal fire safes are designed to prevent paper and similar
materials from being damaged in a fire. They don't prevent computer data,
microfilm/fiche, etc. from being damaged. There's no substitute for redun-
dant copies and off-site backup. 

  As for recovering the data, I suggested trying a TZ30 or a TK70, both of
which are a bit better at reading marginal tapes than a "real" TK50. On the
other hand, you may be better off going right to a recovery house - maybe
trying to read these tapes is damaging them further.

