Ric-

First, check on the QIO ratings of the two.  I wasn't able to find spec's for the
built-in DSSI busses nor the KZQSA Q-bus SCSI adapter.  (Or were you looking at a
third-party Q-bus to SCSI adapter :-) ?)  You may do better to consider one of
Digital's HSDxx DSSI to SCSI controller/converters or a third-party DSSI/SCSI
solution.  DEC's HSD30, for example, will support three SCSI-2 busses with or
without RAID (0,1,3,5).  Of course, you pay for what you get, and if you don't
need nor forsee the future need, why pay?  Third-party solutions are available
from MTI, Invincible Technology, and CMD, amongst others.

Good Luck!

